          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The best electric fireplace for most homes is the <strong class="text-white">Touchstone Sideline 50</strong>: it plugs in, recesses into a standard 2x6 wall and delivers the full 1,500 watts a household outlet allows. Build a mantel around the <strong class="text-white">Dimplex Revillusion</strong> if you want a traditional hearth and more heat on a 240-volt circuit, or skip installation entirely with the <strong class="text-white">Duraflame DFI-5010</strong> stove.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you choose, plan the circuit and the rough opening before you buy, treat the heater as zone heat rather than a furnace replacement, and pick on flame realism and fit, because the heat output of most plug-in models is the same.
